# Line endings are normalised on checkout so the assistant context Markdown composes to the same
# bytes on every machine. The composed brief must stay byte-identical between the web build and the
# native Rust copy (src/studio/assistant/skills.ts and src-tauri/src/assistant_ai.rs); a CRLF
# checkout on a contributor's machine would otherwise change what the normaliser sees.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary assets are never line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.ifc binary
*.dxf binary
*.exe binary
*.tar binary
